Interpretation summary:
  Increasing mu shifts a larger fraction of removed individuals into the deceased compartment.
  The observed final D/R ratio matches mu/gamma for every mu value tested.
  Lowering beta flattens the curve by reducing the infected peak and delaying peak timing.
  Scientific judgment call: prioritize lowering beta first because it directly reduces simultaneous infections and hospital burden; shortening infectious period also lowers R0 but requires rapid detection/isolation/treatment capacity.

